class:: StrongDecay
summary:: Energy weighted toward the start of an observation window
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Amplitude

description::
Computes sqrt(integrated envelope energy / temporal energy centroid). Integrated energy is frameTime * sum(e[i].squared); the centroid uses the same squared RMS weights and frame-centre coordinates. The result increases with signal level and earlier energy. This rolling adaptation follows the energy/temporal-centroid idea described by Gouyon and Herrera (MOSART 2001), with a fully specified RMS-energy convention rather than claimed Essentia equivalence.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression. Source relationship: link::https://essentia.upf.edu/reference/streaming_StrongDecay.html:: describes the Gouyon/Herrera feature family; this implementation defines its own rolling energy convention.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Nonnegative amplitude-like value; not a decay time or normalized probability.

examples::
The measured envelope shape moves the filter and a quiet reference tone; listen as the sample phrases change.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var value = StrongDecay.kr(source, 0.5);
        var control = (value * 5).clip(0, 1);
        var filtered = RLPF.ar(source, control.linexp(0, 1, 250, 4500), 0.25);
        (filtered * 0.25 + SinOsc.ar(control.linexp(0, 1, 150, 650), 0, 0.025))
            * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.7) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
Stop and release the buffer:
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

